public import Theory.SpecificGroups.LieType.F4LongParabolic.BinaryCoordinates
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.IsPerfect

/-!
# Perfectness of the literal binary long-A2 Levi

Each of the four signed simple-root generators is a commutator of two
involutions in the same Levi. The second involution is a conjugate of
another simple-root generator. Checked matrix products establish these
four identities, hence the generated Levi is perfect.

These are the elementary A2 commutator identities, in the Geck coordinates
of `A02ParabolicSections.SourceLevi.F4`; source: GLS3 1.12 and 2.6.
-/
public section
open Subgroup Thompson.BinaryMatrix
open scoped commutatorElement
